{"type":"text","timestamp":1778614647093,"sessionID":"ses_1e25880f2ffeSkLChAGBKhSDcz","part":{"id":"prt_e1db1890800146duIgw3CpJhcI","messageID":"msg_e1db18203001OXWPMlRemTEzpq","sessionID":"ses_1e25880f2ffeSkLChAGBKhSDcz","type":"text","text":"Done! Here's a summary of what was completed for issue #9871:\n\n**Changes made:**\n1. **MONDO:0009106 (diastematomyelia)** — Replaced the too-narrow `Orphanet:1671` (Split cord malformation type I) xref with `Orphanet:573278` (Split cord malformation) as `MONDO:equivalentTo`. Removed the type-1-specific synonyms (\"SCM type 1\" and \"split cord malformation type 1\"). Upgraded \"split cord malformation\" from RELATED to EXACT synonym. Updated all source attributions across subsets, synonyms, and xrefs. Added a term tracker for #9871.\n\n2. **MONDO:0035542 (obsolete split cord malformation)** — Added `replaced_by: MONDO:0009106` so the obsolete term now explicitly points to diastematomyelia. Added a term tracker for #9871.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Terms were checked out, edited, and checked back in properly\n- `make NORM` was run to normalize serialization\n- `robot convert` syntax validation passed with no errors\n- Verified `Orphanet:1671` no longer appears in the ontology\n- Changes committed locally\n\n**Files created (not committed):**\n- `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md` — ready to post back to the GitHub issue\n- `PR_COMMENTS.md` — ready to post back to the originating PR\n\n**Commit:**\n- `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo` updated and committed as `a31e65d` (\"Update Orphanet xref for diastematomyelia (#9871)\")","time":{"start":1778614634760,"end":1778614647092}}}
